  "id": "information-hypothesis",
  "term": "information hypothesis",
  "definition": "In this context, the information hypothesis refers to the affect-as-information view that a person’s or animal’s current mood provides a signal that changes how environmental details are processed. Positive and negative mood states are expected to bias performance differently, including the speed of responding on tasks.",
